=== 00:01 UTC 2026-09-13 PRE-REGISTRATION -- ARM E (review lever L2): a turn-1 workspace survey folded into the prompt, model-free
Motivation (ADR-0161 dumps, ADR-0163 review F2/L2): on 06 as it shipped the 35B spent its first three tool calls on
list_dir (root, plugins, tests) and the 27B the same; every m-task trajectory opens with a listing or a read. Claude
Code opens with `find <ws> -type f`. A capped, ignore-aware survey of the workspace in the system prompt hands every
model that listing for free. Deterministic by construction; the question is what it buys and what it costs.
Design: prompt.py gains `workspace_survey(root, *, max_entries, max_depth)` -- os.walk under the workspace root,
IgnoreSpec-filtered (the same rules list_dir applies: .git, __pycache__, node_modules, venvs, .zakcodeignore/.gitignore),
sorted, depth-capped (3) and count-capped (150 entries; a truncation line states N shown of M). Rendered in the
dynamic tier after the project-context files as "Workspace files (N of M, depth <= 3): ...". Snapshotted ONCE per
builder+workspace (the first build) so the prefix stays byte-stable across the turns of one session: the survey
describes the workspace the task STARTED in; files the agent creates are not re-listed (the model knows what it wrote).
Setting `context_workspace_survey` (env ZAKCODE_CONTEXT_WORKSPACE_SURVEY), default OFF for the arm; ships default-on
only if E1 and E2 hold. Cells: SURVEY vs the ADR-0162/0163 buffered cells (same build otherwise), 35B, N=3, temp 0,
identity, pinned: 06-plugin-conventions, 02-median-bug (the two long trajectories), m01-m05 (control).
Rules:
  E1  outcomes hold on every task (3/3 stays 3/3) -- a survey that flips an outcome is refused, whatever the turns.
  E2  06 and 02 finish in FEWER turns (median) than their reference cells (06: 13, 02: 7), by at least the listing
      calls it replaces (06: >= 2 fewer; 02: >= 1 fewer). Wall time reported but not a rule (pod-minute property).
  E3  m01-m05: outcomes hold; turns must not INCREASE on any task (a survey that distracts a 3-turn task is a cost).
  E4  bytes are expected to CHANGE on every task (the prompt changed); byte identity WITHIN each cell must hold
      (3/3 identical) or the survey is nondeterministic (ordering, mtime leakage) and is refused.
  E5  prompt growth measured from dumps on 06: the survey block's size in chars; must stay < 2,000 chars on these
      workspaces (they are small; the cap is what bounds a real repo).
Prediction: E1 holds; E2 holds on 06 (13 -> 10 or 11) and probably on 02 (7 -> 6); E3 holds; E4 holds; E5 holds.
Verdict rule: E1 & E2 & E3 & E4 -> ship default-on (ADR-0164); E1 & E3 & E4 but not E2 -> keep the setting,
default off, record; any of E1/E3/E4 failing -> refuse.

